# Plan §7b, computed initialization into a Structure-typed place: the bare name of a callable is its call there too --
# the binding's kind decides, not the place (callable-first) -- and b, a Box value, is callable itself: `b: mk` is b's
# call with mk's result as its argument (OPUS-CALLABLE-STRUCT-BINDING-20260929-16), refused where it stands until a
# named Structure's call with an argument is built.  (It was refused as a graph rebinding.)  The explicit reference
# place is unit_local_init_graph_ref_admit_refused.
Box:
    int: v 0
end: Box
fn: mk () Box
    t: merge: Box
    return: t
end: mk
fn: w () int
    b: merge: Box
    b: mk
    return: b\v
end: w
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: w(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
